## PR Title
Fix pytests utils

## PR Description
The PR addresses the `expect_*` methods in utils.py and how they are used in the test suite. The patch makes the tests raise exceptions on mismatches so that failures are actually caught by pytest. The author also notes that parentheses are special regex characters and need to be escaped in the patterns used by these helpers.

The PR is associated with issue #99 which observed that `expect_*` functions were merely returning True/False booleans without actually asserting any condition, so tests using them never failed.

